  <x:String x:Key="Unsplash.ApiKey.Step1">1. Go to Unsplash Developers</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Unsplash.ApiKey.Step2">2. Sign up and create an application</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Unsplash.ApiKey.Step3">3. Copy the Access Key from your app settings</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Unsplash.ApiKey.OpenPortal">🔗 Open Unsplash Developers</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Unsplash.ApiKey.Note">💡 Unsplash API is free with a limit of 50 requests/hour for demo apps.</x:String>
  
  <!-- YouTube API -->
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Title">YouTube API Configuration</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Header">Configure YouTube Data API</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Description">Enter your API key to search videos on YouTube.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Label">YouTube API Key</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Watermark">Enter your YouTube API key...</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.HowToGet">📋 How to get an API key:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Step1">1. Go to Google Cloud Console</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Step2">2. Create a project and enable YouTube Data API v3</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Step3">3. Create an API key in the Credentials section</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.OpenPortal">🔗 Open Google Cloud Console</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="YouTube.ApiKey.Note">💡 YouTube Data API has a free limit of 10,000 units/day.</x:String>

  <!-- User Agreement Window -->
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Title">User Agreement - Vetale Browser</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.TitleView">User Agreement - Vetale Browser (View)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Header">User Agreement</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Welcome">Welcome to Vetale Browser</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Introduction">Before using Vetale Browser, please read and accept this User Agreement. This agreement explains what data we collect and how we use internet services to provide you with the best browsing experience.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.GDPR.Title">GDPR Compliance Notice</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.GDPR.Description">In compliance with the European Union's General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), we are required to inform you about data collection and obtain your consent before processing any personal data.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Components.Title">📊 Components That May Collect Data</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Search.Title">Search Engine Integration (MetaSearx)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Search.Description">Web search is powered by MetaSearx API - an open metasearch engine that aggregates results from Google, Bing, DuckDuckGo, and other search engines. Your queries are processed through metasearx.com.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.AI.Title">AI Chat Services (Vetale AI)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.AI.Description">AI features use Perplexity AI and web versions of other AI services. NO API keys required - the browser works with public web interfaces of AI providers.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Voice.Title">Voice Search (Whisper - Local)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Voice.Description">Voice input is processed LOCALLY on your computer using Whisper. Audio is NOT sent to external servers - all recognition happens offline. Speak for at least 2 seconds for quality recognition. ⚠️ WARNING: Voice search may use any amount of RAM. Use with caution on devices with limited memory.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Web.Title">Web Browsing</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Web.Description">Websites you visit may set cookies and collect data according to their policies. We use CefSharp (Chromium) for web rendering.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Favicon.Title">Favicon Service</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Favicon.Description">Website icons are fetched via external APIs: favicon.im (primary), Google S2 Favicons API, DuckDuckGo Icons API, or directly from the website (/favicon.ico). These services are used to display icons in tabs and bookmarks.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Download.Title">Download Manager</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Download.Description">Files are downloaded directly from source websites. Download history is stored locally on your device.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Title">💾 Data Stored Locally</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Description">The following data is stored only on your device and is not transmitted to any external servers:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Item1">• Browsing history and bookmarks</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Item2">• Browser settings and preferences</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Item3">• Tab sessions for restoration</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Item4">• Console/DevTools logs</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Item5">• Downloaded files metadata</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.LocalStorage.Item6">• Whisper models for local speech recognition</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Title">⚖️ Your Rights Under GDPR</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Description">As a user in the European Union, you have the following rights:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Item1">• Right to access your personal data</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Item2">• Right to rectification of inaccurate data</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Item3">• Right to erasure ("right to be forgotten")</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Item4">• Right to data portability</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Rights.Item5">• Right to withdraw consent at any time</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Disclaimer.Title">⚠️ Disclaimer</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Disclaimer.VetaleSearch">Vetale Search provides image search, video search, and file download functionality. Search results and downloads are NOT filtered or moderated. You have complete freedom of action when using these features.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Disclaimer.NoResponsibility">The developer is NOT responsible for any damage to your system, device, or any other harm caused by your searches or downloads. You use these features at your own risk.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Contact.Title">📧 Contact</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Contact.Description">If you have any questions about this agreement or your data, you can clear all local data through browser settings or contact us through the project repository.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Version">Agreement Version 2.0 | Last Updated: December 2025</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Checkbox">I have read and agree to the terms above</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Decline">Decline</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UserAgreement.Accept">Accept &amp; Continue</x:String>

  <!-- VetaleSearch Settings Page -->
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Header">Vetale Search Settings</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.ApiKeys.Title">API Keys</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.ApiKeys.Description">Enter your API keys for each service. Keys are stored locally and encrypted. You need these keys to use image search, video search, and AI features.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Gemini.Watermark">Enter your Gemini API key...</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Pexels.Watermark">Enter your Pexels API key...</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Unsplash.Watermark">Enter your Unsplash Access Key...</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.YouTube.Watermark">Enter your YouTube API key...</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Appearance.Title">Appearance</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Appearance.Description">Customize the colors used on the Vetale Search pages.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.GradientStart">Gradient start color:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.GradientEnd">Gradient end color:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.CardBackground">Card background color:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.LinkColor">Link color:</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="VetaleSearch.Settings.Note">Your API keys are stored locally with encryption and never sent to our servers. You can get free API keys from the services above.</x:String>
  
